1. VERDICTS

C1 | EFFECT-NOT-EXISTENCE | CONTRADICTED (partially) — the plan is mostly effect-graded, but 19 of its 284 rows grade existence or log-strings, and two of them are exactly where the incident happened.
Evidence: my census over the 284 `command` fields (grep/test/wc-shaped, no side-effect verb): 22 rows; overlapping the brief's 19. Named existence-only/marker rows: C-036, C-039, C-066 (cmd), C-067, C-076, C-096, C-163, C-191, C-192, C-231, C-236, C-268, plus census/hygiene rows C-180/C-227 (acceptable). The 193 "unclassified" do NOT hide a second population of greps — I sampled ~30 and they are real curl/sqlite3/bun/make behaviour commands — but the false-green risk migrates from command to pass_criteria there ("result present" C-092, "error field present" C-095, "all three" C-110). Rewrites: C-036 → "committed results.tsv has ≥4 suite rows, Classification≠SETUP_FAILURE, Σ tests>0" (today C-036's two greps both PASS against the void run's committed summary.md:5-6 — measured); C-039/C-163/C-268 → "count of crier-origin user_message rows with provenance > 0 in DB after a delivered message" (and C-163/C-268 are duplicate greps of the same thing — convergence amplified an existence check); C-076 → assert assistant message rows + billing rows in DB, not log strings; C-191 → assert pool behavior (max_open_conns=5 in effect), not a commit hash in history.
Why: the two T6 provenance greps and the three crier greps grade artifacts the runner or a future commit writes — the exact (a)/(b) shape that closed C-GAP-032-ALPHA.

C2 | FALSE-GREEN EXPOSURE | CONTRADICTED — of the six named guards, exactly one is executable as written, and it cannot fail correctly.
Evidence (command texts, manifest): C-122 "re-read board… emit GREEN/RED/VOID" — prose, no executable body. C-123 "for each tier: assert its primary counter > 0" — prose, and no field declares any tier's "primary counter". C-284 "build single-file HTML" — prose. C-187 and C-230 call `scripts/battery/…` — that directory does not exist (measured `ls scripts/battery/` → No such file; same for rederive.sh, t7_roundtrip.sh, t9_load.sh, t3_agent_chain.sh referenced by C-206/C-219/C-226). C-124 runs but its rc semantics are inverted (grep exits 1 on a CLEAN bundle, 0 on a leak) and its pattern `sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}` misses consensus's own `cs_ak_`/`cs_sk_` keys, which the runner's own sanitizer (test-opencode-upstream.sh sanitize()) does redact. C-231 ends `; echo rc=$?` → always exits 0; it cannot fail. The incident is proof-by-demonstration: a closed testing task with 0 executed tests passed all six guards.
Why: guards that are declarations block nothing; a guard whose exit code lies is worse than none.

C3 | EXECUTABILITY AS WRITTEN | CONTRADICTED — 200+ command slots reference variables the plan never defines; the guard scripts don't exist.
Measured: `$RUN_ROOT` ×117, `$SRV` ×24, `$EV` ×22, `$BASE` ×17, `$KEY` ×14, `$RUN_ID` ×6, `$ADMIN_KEY` ×6, `$RUN` ×3, `$S1–$S4` ×9, `$TARGET_SHA` (self-referential only), `$B` ×1 — zero assignments anywhere in plan or manifest (grep `RUN_ROOT=` = 0; plan mentions of RUN_ROOT/TARGET_SHA/$EV/$BASE = 0). Only `$LOAD1` (C-051) is defined inline. Tools: yq MISSING on the control host (C-067); C-238 installs `golang-go nodejs npm` on the bunker but T6 needs `bun` (not installed) and egress; `sqlite3` used 19× but absent on a bare bunker; C-099 assumes an `opencode` CLI on PATH. Paths: `scripts/prove-opencode-cli.sh` exists ✓; `scripts/battery/*.sh` (4 refs) ✗ none exist. Contradiction: C-238 pins the bunker checkout at 77b990b while C-001 requires HEAD == `$TARGET_SHA` — two different pinned SHAs in one plan.
Why: a step that cannot run as written is a step a runner will silently skip — class (d) is baked into the environment block.

C4 | DECIDABILITY | CONTRADICTED — 189/284 pass_criteria carry neither a digit nor an operator word by my regex (strict subset genuinely undecidable, worst named below).
Undecidable as written, with replacements: C-015 "All DB/API assertions true" → enumerate the assertion ids; C-024 "Nonce and result semantics present" → `result.rows_affected==39 and nonce in result JSON`; C-033 "IDs cross-check through REST and DB" → `id set from GET == id set from sqlite query, count>0`; C-039 → see C1; C-065 "both absent, recorded" → `test ! -e <path> for each of the 2 named paths`; C-092 "result present" → `jq '.result != null'`; C-095 "error field present" → `jq '.error.code == <expected>'`; C-096 "exact strings" → `diff <(grep -E ...) <(printf ...)`; C-100 "recorded only; must NOT be cited" → that is an instruction to a report writer, not a check — convert to a report-lint; C-110 "all three" → name the three.
Why: "present" without a locator is a vibe with a checkbox.

C5 | SURFACE COVERAGE | ACCEPTED with named gaps.
Mapping: real LLM answers → T2 (30, verified live: sweep row "live answer 391, billing 0.009805"); real agent loops → T2 multi-turn + T3 (strong: C-206/C-251 hard `tool_requests>0`); real session tracking → T4 (28 rows on paper, but the sweep's T4 was covered only by the T2 smoke and its own rows are alarming: ledger-types FAIL types={}, billing-rows FAIL 0 rows, and "session-tokens" marked PASS with observed `('failed', 0, 0)` — the runner already false-greens, tier-sweep-v2.json:124-128); tool calls → T3 covered, but sweep shows audit path rows=0 (tool_results audit gap); baby projects → T10 covered and best-shaped (disk + nonce), currently failing on a real 400; MCP for an arbitrary agent → T5 cannot pass today (measured /mcp 404, POST /mcp/message 400 even with sessionId) and MCP-DIRECT-001 was closed by README docs — documentation is not discoverability; crier messages → T7 is phantom by construction (zero code; CR-IN-001 pending, P2) and its 32 rows cannot discharge the owner's ask until it lands. UNDER-COVERED overall: T4 (never really run), T5 (arbitrary-agent attach has zero measured PASS), T7 (absent), T6 (void evidence), T9 (unrun). The owner's ask is currently provable only for: LLM answers, multi-turn, tool execute, install.
Why: 284 rows overstate coverage; the ask is discharged by ~4 tiers today.

C6 | SUBGOAL CONVERTIBILITY | ACCEPTED — sketches for the three most false-green-prone tiers (T6, T4, T7), smallest decisive first:

SG-1 Prove the upstream runner executes tests, not setups
  done-when: `sh scripts/test-opencode-upstream.sh --base-url http://127.0.0.1:<shim-port>` exits 0 AND the committed results.tsv has ≥4 suite rows with Classification != SETUP_FAILURE AND sum(tests column) > 0 — checked by `awk -F'\t' 'END{exit !(NR>=4 && s>0 && f==0)} {s+=$4; if($7=="SETUP_FAILURE")f++}' results.tsv`
