  depends-on: none
  falsifier: all four suites classify SETUP_FAILURE (bun/checkout/transport missing on the bunker) → C-GAP-032-ALPHA stays open, T6 reported PARTIAL, "upstream-verified" claim dies — this subgoal can kill the plan early, which is why it is first.

SG-2 One live turn produces ledger + billing rows with exact counts
  done-when: after 1 real round trip, `sqlite3 $DB "select count(*) from memory_events where session_id='<sid>'"` ≥ 3 AND `select count(*) from agent_billing where session_id='<sid>'` ≥ 1 with cost_usd > 0 AND billing model == served model, all asserted in one command chain that exits nonzero on any count==0
  evidence: $EV/t4/ledger-billing.json + the sqlite dump
  depends-on: none (independent of SG-1; needs the S1 key preflight)
  falsifier: LLM call count != billing row count (the 1:1 check C-259) or cost re-derivation off the registry by >10% → the billing-table-vs-bill confusion (31.9x class) is live and T4 is not green.

SG-3 One crier-delivered message becomes an agent-visible user turn
  done-when: deliver via crier against live consensus → `sqlite3 $DB "select count(*) from memory_events where session_id='<sid>' and type='user_message' and provenance like 'crier:%'"` == 1 AND ack drains inbox (`queue_depth == 0` in GET stats)
  evidence: $EV/t7/intake-proof.json (delivery receipt + DB row dump)
