C7 | REPEAT-OFFENSE | CONTRADICTED — the artifact re-arms every named failure class:
(a)/(b) built/existence read as done: C-036, C-039, C-163, C-268, C-192, C-191.
(c) success-marker string checks: C-036 (greps a runner-written summary), C-076 (greps "llm: response received"), C-191.
(d) silent-skip: the undefined `$RUN_ROOT` family (C3) makes ~200 steps unrunnable-as-written; C-163's "else tier BLOCKED" has no machine rule propagating BLOCKED into the gate.
(e) green-but-did-nothing: C-231 always exits 0; C-124's rc is inverted for the clean case; C-187/C-230 would exit 127 (command-not-found) on the missing scripts — an rc a naive runner can misread.
(f) bar-lowering: defect_gate uses "-" placeholders (31 rows) that the brief's own census counted as "set" (see Corrections #6); C-263's escape hatch "or EXPECTED-FAIL MCP-DIRECT-001" now points at a CLOSED row (board: complete, df33c39) so any T5 failure files against a closed id. Credential paths: `$KEY`/`$ADMIN_KEY` used 20× with no provisioning story, and the plan's secret scan does not know consensus's own key shapes (cs_ak_/cs_sk_) — the evidence bundle could leak a bootstrap key invisibly.

C8 | THE INCIDENT | ACCEPTED (mechanism named; single change identified).
Mechanism: the plan binds no executor to the manifest and no closure check to artifacts. Closure authority lived in the tick's narration — board event 396 claims "sdk-error-shape 2/2 PASS, client promise 7/7 PASS, instance 3/7 PASS, SDK 16/18 PASS", and I measured `git grep '16/18' HEAD` → those numbers exist ONLY in board files, in no evidence artifact; the committed summary.md says tests=unknown, pass=0, fail=0 with 189-byte setup-failure logs. Meanwhile the plan's own T6 existence check C-036 greps that same summary for the revision string and "Lock SHA-256" — both present (summary.md:5-6) — so the plan's T6 provenance test PASSES on the void run. Nothing in the manifest parses results.tsv (which didn't exist yet) or asserts executed>0 at closure time; §6's re-derivation rule applies at report time, which never came.
The single change: make C-123 (VOID detection) executable against committed artifacts and run it as a precondition of board closure — i.e., a committed checker re-derives each tier's counter from $EV (for T6: Σ tests > 0 and 0 SETUP_FAILURE rows in results.tsv) and refuses the close. That converts §6's report-time rule into a closure-time gate and makes the C-GAP-032-ALPHA closure mechanically impossible.

